{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "Symptoms of folliculitis in adolescents: diagnosis and confirmation of causative organisms in skin lesions.", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T19:25:24.040523+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "Folliculitis - Symptoms and causes - Mayo Clinic", "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/folliculitis/symptoms-causes/syc-20361634+", "snippet": "Aug 31, 2022 · Folliculitis is a common skin condition that happens when hair follicles become inflamed. It's often caused by an infection with bacteria. At first it may look like small pimples around the tiny pockets from where each hair grows (hair follicles). The condition can be itchy, sore and embarrassing."}, {"title": "Folliculitis - Infectious Disease - Merck Manual Professional ...", "url": "https://www.merckmanuals.com/professional/infectious-diseases/bacterial-skin-infections/folliculitis", "snippet": "Symptoms of folliculitis include mild pain, pruritus, and irritation. A sign of folliculitis is a superficial pustule or inflammatory nodule surrounding a hair follicle. Hairs in infected follicles fall out easily or may be removed by the patient, but new pustules tend to develop."}, {"title": "Folliculitis Clinical Presentation: History, Physical ...", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/1070456-clinical", "snippet": "Apr 22, 2014 · Patients with deep folliculitis usually have longer-standing lesions and more often report pain and (sometimes) suppurative drainage. Persistent or recurrent lesions may result in scarring..."}]}
