{"status": "ok", "backend": "ddgs-auto", "query": "Lab abnormalities indicating treatment in a 50-year-old sedentary male with hypertension and high cholesterol.", "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T19:24:57.587165+00:00", "documents": [{"title": "Hypertension Workup: Approach Considerations, Baseline ...", "url": "https://emedicine.medscape.com/article/241381-workup", "snippet": "May 27, 2026 · Electrocardiogram (ECG) from a 46-year-old man with long-standing hypertension. This ECG shows left atrial abnormality and left ventricular hypertrophy with strain."}, {"title": "Blood tests for heart disease - Mayo ClinicMen Over the Age of 50 Should Consider These 9 Lab Tests Done ...Essential Lab Tests for Men Over 50: Your Proactive Health ...Hypertension Evaluation Labs - FPnotebook.comHigh cholesterol - Diagnosis and treatment - Mayo Clinic", "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/heart-disease/in-depth/heart-disease/art-20049357", "snippet": "A cholesterol test, also called a lipid panel or lipid profile, measures the fats in the blood. The results can show the risk of having a heart attack or other heart disease. The test most often measures: 1. Total cholesterol. This is the amount of the blood's cholesterol content. A high level can raise the risk of heart disease. It's best if the t... See full list on mayoclinic.org The liver makes C-reactive protein (CRP) as part of the body's response to injury or infection. The response causes swelling inside the body, called inflammation. Inflammation plays a major role in the buildup of plaques in the arteries, called atherosclerosis. High-sensitivity CRP (hs-CRP) tests help show the risk of heart disease before there are... See full list on mayoclinic.org Lipoprotein (a), or Lp(a), is a type of LDL cholesterol. Genes affect Lp(a)level. Lifestyle does not. High levels of Lp(a) may show a higher risk of heart disease. But it's not clear how much risk. Your health care professional might order an Lp(a)test if you have atherosclerosis or heart disease but seem to have healthy cholesterol levels. Or you ... See full list on mayoclinic.org This test measures the levels of ceramides in the blood. All cells make ceramides. They play a big role in the way many types of tissue grow, work and die. Ceramides are linked to atherosclerosis. Three ceramides have been linked to plaque buildup in the arteries and insulin resistance, which can lead to type 2 diabetes. High levels of these cerami... See full list on mayoclinic.org Brain natriuretic peptide is a protein the heart and blood vessels make. It's also called B-type natriuretic peptide (BNP). BNPhelps the body get rid of fluids, relaxes blood vessels and moves sodium into the urine. With heart damage, the body puts high levels of BNP into the blood to try to ease the strain on the heart. One important use of BNPis ... See full list on mayoclinic.org Troponin T is a protein found in heart muscle. A high-sensitivity troponin T test helps health care professionals diagnose a heart attack. The test also shows the risk of heart disease. An increased level of troponin T has been linked with a higher risk of heart disease in people who have no symptoms. See full list on mayoclinic.org Nov 18, 2024 · Annual lab testing for men over 50 is an important aspect of preventive health care to detect and manage chronic diseases, enhance quality of life, and promote longevity. Nov 18, 2025 · Modern lab testing gives you 24–48 hour insight into thyroid conversion, hidden inflammation, hormone balance, and metabolic health — years before a disease label shows up. This page includes the following topics and synonyms: Hypertension Evaluation Labs, Hypertension Diagnostic Testing. Mar 7, 2025 · Learn more about the diagnosis and treatment of High cholesterol. Find tips to get ready for any appointments you need."}, {"title": "Men Over the Age of 50 Should Consider These 9 Lab Tests Done ...", "url": "https://www.rupahealth.com/post/men-over-the-age-of-50-should-consider-these-9-lab-tests-done-yearly", "snippet": "Nov 18, 2024 · Annual lab testing for men over 50 is an important aspect of preventive health care to detect and manage chronic diseases, enhance quality of life, and promote longevity."}]}
